As I understand it, in the BPFK thread {lo nu broda ba brode}, a=20
majority of people voiced in favor of {lo nu broda ba brode} to become=20
equal to {lo nu broda cu ba brode}. I don't think this entails by itself=20
that {broda be ba brode} is no longer grammatical.
But if a clarification on that point is needed, we can have the BPFK=20
vote on whether {broda be ba brode} should be grammatical or not.

